 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 631794,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>For the following exercise, consider this scenario: For each year <span data-math=\"t\">t</span>, the population of trees in Forest A is represented by the function <span data-math=\"A(t)=115(1.025)^t\">A(t)=115(1.025)^t</span>, (red curve). In a neighboring forest, Forest B, the population of the same type of tree is represented by the function <span data-math=\"B(t)=82(1.029)^t\">B(t)=82(1.029)^t</span>, (blue curve). Looking at the graph provided, which forest had a greater number of trees initially?</p>\n<p><img alt=\"GRAPH OF TWO EXPONENTIAL FUNCTIONS. THE FUNCTION A OF T IN RED HAS A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 115. THE FUNCTION OF B OF T IN BLUE HAS A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 82.&nbsp;\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"285\" src=\"exercises/media/234f8662d2cdb79a.jpg\" width=\"300\"></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222786,
     "content_html": "Forest B, because it has a greater growth rate."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222785,
     "content_html": "Forest A, because it has a greater growth rate."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222787,
     "content_html": "Forest A, because it starts higher on the <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-axis."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222784,
     "content_html": "Both forests started with the same number of trees."
    }
   ],
